[N 15-16 Hall of Thanes]
[D Forever Shaman 1-30 (Braedyn)\\The new Ironforge dungeon (finder level 13, quests 15-16): pickups, the run with normal/grind labels per quest, loot to roll on, hand-ins.]
[GA Alliance]
[OC]|cffffffffIronforge - Hall of Thanes|r  -  5 quests, ~6,050 XP, and the Ironforge Greathammer
[OC]|cffffcc00Bring:|r your friend + 3 more (level 15-17 is comfortable). Water, and Stoneskin/Searing totems for the pulls.

[OC]|cffffffffIronforge errands first|r
In the Hall of Explorers at [TAR1356 Prospector Stormpike], [QT301] [QA302 Powder to Ironband] [G74.6,11.7 Ironforge]
[A Shaman] In the Forlorn Cavern at [TAR258098 Eldrun Stormbreaker], [T] train - make sure you have Searing Totem [G47.1,13.8 Ironforge]
[A Hunter] In the Military Ward at [TAR5116 Olmin Burningbeard], [T] train (level 14: Eyes of the Beast, Eagle Eye, Scare Beast), then [TAR5123 Bretta Goldfury] (72.2,65.2): Dwarves top up Heavy Shot (400+ for the dungeon); Humans still on the bow buy a Small Shot Pouch and 600 Heavy Shot now - the reward at the end of this dungeon is a gun [G72.2,65.2 Ironforge]
[OC][A Hunter] In the dungeon: pet on passive until the tank has the pack, then send it at the tank's target; you have no threat drop yet, so if you pull threat stop shooting for a moment. Feed the pet before you zone in.
[OC]In the Commons, [R][V] and stock 20+ water [G34,60 Ironforge]
[OC]|cffffcc00Camping 101 hand-ins:|r if Skinning is 20+, [TAR6291 Balthus Stoneflayer] (Skinning trainer, 39.9,32.5) completes Camping 101: Skinning and teaches the Camp Chair; Leatherworking 20+ = Gretta Finespindle next to him (Camp Tent = rested XP); Mining 20+ = Yarr Hammerstone in Kharanos (Lodestone); First Aid 20+ = Thamner Pol in Kharanos (First Aid Kit). If First Aid or Cooking is already 50, Nissa Firestone (55.1,58.3) and Daryl Riknussun (60.1,36.4) teach Journeyman.
At [TAR5159 Daryl Riknussun] (east side of the Great Forge), learn Journeyman Cooking NOW if you still have not - this is your last Ironforge stop before Marek's Crocolisk Steak recipe (Cooking 80) in the 16-17 chapter, and Apprentice stops at 75. Short of 50? Cook your boar meat, ribs and Longjaw at his fire until you are there [T] [G60.1,36.4 Ironforge]
[O]In the Forlorn Cavern at [TAR5161 Grimnur Stonebrand], learn Journeyman Fishing if Fishing is 50 [T] [G48.1,6.9 Ironforge]
[O]At [TAR5150 Nissa Firestone], learn Journeyman First Aid (and Heavy Linen) if you were short of 50 in chapter 2 [T] [G55.1,58.3 Ironforge]


[OC]|cffffcc00Pre-dungeon quest log:|r
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r The Restless Dead (96394) - Afadra Dunwall, 32.4,47.8
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Important Heirlooms (96403) - Thom Filch, 31.4,45.4
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Old Ironforge Incursion (96393) - from Earthseer Farsen in Dun Morogh after the Underground Map
[OC]Starts inside: An Ancient Grudge (Ghostly Attendant), The Treaty of Understanding (tablet in the last room)
[OC]If you missed them: Afadra Dunwall (32.4,47.8) and Thom Filch (31.4,45.4) stand between the Commons and the Mystic Ward

[OC]|cffffffffThe run|r
[OC]|cffffcc00Camp before you zone in:|r at the portal, one of you drops a Basic Campfire (Cooking), then everyone adds one profession object (your Lodestone or Camp Chair, your friend's) and sits 1 minute - the buffs last an hour, about one run
[OC]Entrance: go into the High Seat (Magni's throne room), take the passage on the LEFT of the throne down into Old Ironforge; the Hall of Thanes portal is at the bottom [G39,55 Ironforge]
[OC]|cffffcc00Quest labels:|r Restless Dead = |cff66ff66normal|r (the ghosts are the trash of the first wing). Important Heirlooms = |cff66ff66normal|r (8 relics you click as you go; ask the group to leave them, and clear the wing if you are short). Ancient Grudge = |cff66ff66normal|r (boss 1). Old Ironforge Incursion = |cff66ff66normal|r (boss 4). Treaty = |cff66ff66normal|r (tablet behind a door in the last room).
[OC]|cffffffffWest wing|r
Just inside, talk to the [TAR265002 Ghostly Attendant], [QA96395 An Ancient Grudge]
[O]|cff66ff66Ongoing:|r kill 15 [TAR263389 Enraged Apparition] and 10 [TAR263390 Tormented Soul] in the first wing [QC96394]
[O]|cff66ff66Ongoing:|r click 8 Dwarven Heirlooms (relics on the floor and shelves through the whole dungeon) [QC96403]
[OC]|cffffffffBoss 1 - Faldrim Anvilmar|r (undead, Anvilmar's Rest, the big central room)
[OC]Tank and spank. Mind Blast on random targets; Anvilmar's Curse petrifies and cuts attack speed 20% - stay near the tank so it only lands on him, and keep threat steady
Kill [TAR261306 Faldrim Anvilmar] [QC96395]
[OC]|cffffcc00Loot:|r Spiritwraith Drape (back +3 Agi +4 Spi) - roll. Ephemeral Choker (neck +5 Spi) - roll, it is the only neck for ten levels. Aetherwisp Bracers - cloth caster, pass.
Back at the [TAR265002 Ghostly Attendant], [QT96395]
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Gear:|r take Deepgrave Trousers (leather legs +3 Agi +3 Spi - they lost their Strength in the October builds); Catacomb Cloak (+2 Sta +3 AP, +4 more against humanoids) is still behind, 5.5 vs 3.0
[OC][A Hunter] |cffffcc00Gear:|r Deepgrave Trousers here too (the Agi and Spirit carry it) - swap to Direhammer Leggings if Durgen drops them

[OC]|cffffffffBoss 2 - Magmatus|r (fire elemental with a Dark Iron Summoner add)
[OC]Trash on the way: Dark Iron Summoners (fireballs - kill first), Engineers (throw dynamite), Bloodhound Runts (their bite is a disease, +6% damage taken - Cure Disease comes at 18, so heal through it), Dark Iron Looters (fast dagger hits)
[OC]Combust is a 360 degree AoE around the boss: tank faces him away, melee stand spread and step out when he winds up
Kill [TAR261316 Magmatus]
[OC]|cffffcc00Loot:|r Flamefist Grips (leather hands +5 Agi +5 Spi) - roll, best gloves in the bracket. Kindlegem Girdle is mail, Fang of Magmatus is a caster dagger - pass.

[OC]|cffffffffBoss 3 - Plunder|r (stone golem)
[OC]Knock Away knockback AoE and a charge that stuns a random player. Fight him in the tunnel you came through so the knockbacks push you into a wall, not into the next pack. Do not pull adds into him.
Kill [TAR261311 Plunder]
[OC]|cffffcc00Loot:|r Golemheart Stave (2H staff, spell power) only if you plan to level Elemental; Golemguard Chest and Treads are mail - pass.

[OC]|cffffffffBoss 4 - Durgen Dirgehammer|r (the Dark Iron commander, 2 Lesser Stone Golems + Looters)
[OC]Kill the two golems first (they hit hard and move fast), then Durgen. He fears the group and Rends - nobody has a fear break at this level, so let the tank re-grab him after it and heal up afterwards.
Kill [TAR261319 Durgen Dirgehammer] and loot his head [QC96393]
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Loot:|r Durgen's Crescent Axe (1H axe 12.3 dps +4 Str) only for a shield set; Direhammer Leggings (+4 Agi +7 Sta) are worse than your Deepgrave Trousers; Robes of the Disgraced Thane is cloth - pass.
[OC][A Hunter] |cffffcc00Loot:|r |cff66ff66Direhammer Leggings|r (leather +4 Agi +7 Sta) - ROLL, they beat Deepgrave Trousers for you. Durgen's Crescent Axe (1H axe 12.3 dps +2 Str +1 Agi) is a fine stat stick if your melee slot is still the starting weapon. Robes of the Disgraced Thane is cloth - pass.
Behind one of the doors in the last room, click the stone tablet, [QA98423 The Treaty of Understanding]
Finish the heirlooms and ghosts before you leave [QC96403] [QC96394]

[OC]|cffffffffHand-ins|r
At [TAR265003 Thom Filch], [QT96403] [G31.4,45.4 Ironforge]
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Gear:|r take Tomb Robber's Gloves (+1 Sta +2 Int) only as a bag filler - Flamefist Grips are better; the Dwarven Tome is an off-hand you cannot use with a 2H
[OC][A Hunter] |cffffcc00Gear:|r nothing (cloth gloves / held item) - Tomb Robber's Gloves to vendor
At [TAR264943 Afadra Dunwall], [QT96394] [G32.4,47.8 Ironforge]
[OC]|cffffcc00Gear:|r take Dusty Belt (leather waist +2 Agi +2 Spi) - Cryptwalker Bracers are mail
In the High Seat at [TAR2784 King Magni Bronzebeard], [QT96393] [QT98423] [G39.4,55.4 Ironforge]
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Gear:|r take |cff66ff66Ironforge Greathammer|r (2H mace 16.0 dps with a fire proc - no stats, no level requirement) and equip it - your weapon until Deadmines
[OC][A Hunter] |cffffcc00Gear:|r take |cff66ff66Calibrated Blunderbuss|r (gun 15.9 dps +3 Sta, no level requirement) and equip it - your gun until well past 20; Heavy Shot fits it
[OC]|cffffffffLevel 16|r
At [TAR1573 Gryth Thurden], |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Thelsamar]|r for the Loch Modan leftovers [G55.5,47.7 Ironforge]
